1. NEW IMPLEMENTATION  (mcp_server/mesh_analysis.py L1221-1290)
================================================================================
Signature / return type UNCHANGED:
  def _snap_group_vertices(welded_verts, tri_indices, welded_tris, snap_tol)
  -> Dict[int, int]  ({old_vertex_index: canonical_vertex_index})

Body change (only the merge loop; guard, vi_set/vi_list build, _find with path
compression, remap build, return are byte-identical to the pre-change version):

    snap_sq = snap_tol * snap_tol
    cells: Dict[Tuple[int, int, int], List[int]] = defaultdict(list)
    for i in range(n):
        p = coords[i]
        cell = (int(math.floor(p[0] / snap_tol)),
                int(math.floor(p[1] / snap_tol)),
                int(math.floor(p[2] / snap_tol)))
        for dx in (-1, 0, 1):
            for dy in (-1, 0, 1):
                for dz in (-1, 0, 1):
                    for u in cells.get((cell[0] + dx, cell[1] + dy,
                                        cell[2] + dz), ()):
                        diff = coords[i] - coords[u]
                        if float(diff @ diff) < snap_sq:
                            ri, rj = _find(u), _find(i)
                            if ri != rj:
                                if ri < rj:
                                    parent[rj] = ri
                                else:
                                    parent[ri] = rj
        cells[cell].append(i)

Algorithm:
- Cell size = snap_tol; cell key = (floor(x/snap_tol), floor(y/snap_tol),
  floor(z/snap_tol))  [per plan spec — floor, NOT round() like _cluster_near_vertices].
- Each vertex is inserted into its own cell only AFTER probing, so every candidate
  u in a probed cell has u < i  (mirrors the old outer-i/inner-j>i ordering).
- Probe = 27-cell neighbourhood (dx,dy,dz in {-1,0,1}) → every in-range pair found.
- Union predicate unchanged: float((coords[i]-coords[u]) @ (coords[i]-coords[u]))
  < snap_sq  (strict <, same float64 op order: high-index minus low-index, then
  dx*dx+dy*dy+dz*dz).
- Union rule unchanged: smaller root absorbs larger (parent[max(ri,rj)] = min(ri,rj)).
- Determinism: defaultdict insertion order is stable; per-cell lists append in
  ascending index order; canonical root = smallest vertex index per cluster
  (order-independent, see §3).

